{"slug":"cactus-whistle-16mb-speech","title":"Whistle fits speech recognition into 16.9 MB","narration":"Cactus Compute squeezed speech recognition into a 16.9-megabyte file that runs without a GPU. Whistle is built for phones, wearables, robots, cars and even microcontrollers, handling seven languages entirely on-device. It transcribes up to 30 seconds per pass, can return word timestamps, and shares the same CPU engine as Cactus’s Needle model. That means one tiny runtime can hear audio, turn it into text, then pass it into local tools. The tradeoff is obvious: this is not a giant cloud model pretending your watch is a data center. It is deliberately small, quantized and specialized. Tiny speech models are getting suspiciously useful.","beats":[{"text":"Cactus Compute squeezed speech recognition","editorialRole":"setup","visual":{"type":"source","sourceIndex":0,"query":"Cactus Whistle speech recognition model","mustMatch":["whistle"]},"sfx":"whoosh"},{"text":"into a 16.9-megabyte file","editorialRole":"reaction","visual":{"type":"metric","value":"16.9 MB"},"memeIntent":{"purpose":"reaction","tone":"surprised","intensity":2,"preferredMedia":"image","presentation":"overlay","maxDurationSeconds":0.9,"concepts":["tiny","small","reaction"]}},{"text":"that runs without a GPU.","editorialRole":"punchline","visual":{"type":"kinetic","text":"NO GPU","emphasis":"NO GPU"},"memeIntent":{"purpose":"success","tone":"positive","intensity":1,"preferredMedia":"image","presentation":"overlay","maxDurationSeconds":0.9,"concepts":["no gpu","nice","reaction"]}},{"text":"Whistle is built for phones, wearables, robots, cars","editorialRole":"fact","visual":{"type":"source","sourceIndex":0,"query":"Whistle phones wearables robots cars","mustMatch":["whistle"],"allowReuse":true}},{"text":"and even microcontrollers,","editorialRole":"fact","visual":{"type":"source","sourceIndex":0,"query":"Whistle microcontrollers on device","mustMatch":["microcontrollers","whistle"],"allowReuse":true}},{"